WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.520
- What proof do you have
that the earth is flat?

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:05.970
- With my own eyes, I have seen distances

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:09.420
where we shouldn't have
been able to see objects.

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:12.360
- If you were alone in a
room with a flat earther,

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:13.530
what would you ask?

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:16.560
- How would one prove
that the earth is flat?

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:19.260
- Why would NASA and these scientists

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:20.730
lie to us about it?

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:23.463
- Yes, that is like the
million dollar question.

00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:26.850
- Hello, I'm Pamela.

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:27.683
Nice to meet you.

00:00:27.683 --> 00:00:29.220
- Hi, I'm Shelley, nice to meet you.

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:31.800
- Did someone convince you
that the earth is flat?

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:32.633
- Well, I wouldn't say

00:00:32.633 --> 00:00:35.370
that someone actually convinced
me the earth was flat.

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:38.700
- So why would NASA and these scientists

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:40.230
lie to us about to us about it?

00:00:40.230 --> 00:00:43.170
- Yes, that is like the
million dollar question.

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:46.260
I think that they're doing
it to maybe protect us

00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:48.690
from something that
they think is out there

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:50.070
that they don't want us to know.

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:51.780
I have my hypothesis is that I think

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:55.500
that they're hiding the
true creation of this earth.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:57.960
- How do you think the earth was created?

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:00.090
- I believe the Bible when it talks

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:02.610
about the earth was created in seven days,

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:06.000
he created a firmament
and he created the sun

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.790
and the moon and the stars
inside of the firmament.

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:12.270
- What I guess proof do you
have that the earth is flat?

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:15.960
- With my own eyes, I
have seen distances where

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:18.540
we shouldn't have been
able to see objects.

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:22.350
- Could you describe
the shape of the earth,

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:24.960
like a piece of paper or a plate?

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:28.560
- The best way I can describe
it is it's like a circle

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:32.160
like a clock with a
dome over the top of it.

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:34.380
- So where do you believe
the earth ends then?

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:37.200
If you believe it's flat, like
where is the fall off point?

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:39.930
- It could be like an infinite plane.

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:41.520
The Bible says it can't be measured.

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:43.920
I know that's not
scientific, but you know,

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:46.680
that's just kind of what
we've experienced as well.

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:49.770
Even going back to what Elon
Musk had said at one point

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:52.440
not that I believe
everything Elon Musk says,

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:54.000
but it was interesting and intriguing

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:56.700
to me of what he said was that we live

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:57.900
in a simulation.

00:01:57.900 --> 00:01:59.370
- There's a one in billions chance

00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:00.660
that this is based reality.

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:03.900
- How many people would
I guess be in on it?

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:07.770
- Very few people, high
up people are in the know.

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:09.360
- How do you feel about the pictures

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:11.040
of the earth from space?

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:14.340
- If you look at those
pictures, NASA will even admit

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:17.940
that their CGI and even a
gentlemen from NASA said

00:02:17.940 --> 00:02:19.980
that some of the pictures that they get

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:22.560
from satellites are these composite images

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:24.300
that they have to kind of paste together.

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:26.610
And so it's hard for me to say

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:30.540
with all certainty that
those pictures are authentic.

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:32.940
- Do you think the moon landing was fake?

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:33.773
- Yes.

00:02:33.773 --> 00:02:34.770
- What led you to believe that?

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:38.730
- So my husband actually
brought home this movie talking

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:40.950
about how the moon landing was fake

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:43.860
and I honestly was like so upset

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:46.170
that he would even go there with me.

00:02:46.170 --> 00:02:47.880
I started to question it more.

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:50.640
Sure enough, there's absolutely no way

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:52.350
that they could have gone to the moon.

00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:53.370
Absolutely.

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:54.360
- Honestly, I agree.

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:55.193
- Oh, you do?

00:02:55.193 --> 00:02:56.583
- I do agree yes.

00:02:58.350 --> 00:03:00.326
Tell me what you think.

00:03:00.326 --> 00:03:01.159
- Just the way it was depicted.

00:03:01.159 --> 00:03:03.510
It really never connected in my mind.

00:03:03.510 --> 00:03:04.980
- I was not expecting you.

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:07.740
- Yeah.
that's cool.

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:10.830
- How do you explain like
the phases of the moon?

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:14.550
- We believe that the
moon is its own light.

00:03:14.550 --> 00:03:15.940
A lot of people think

00:03:16.825 --> 00:03:19.860
that the sun basically
reflects onto the moon,

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:24.090
but what we find is that the
moonlight is a cooler light

00:03:24.090 --> 00:03:26.040
and the sun is more of a hot light.

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:30.660
- So if the earth is flat,
how do you explain time zones?

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:32.550
- So if it's a close sun,

00:03:32.550 --> 00:03:34.380
it would be kind of like a spotlight.

00:03:34.380 --> 00:03:36.870
The time zones work
because that local light

00:03:36.870 --> 00:03:38.610
just kind of like a flashlight,

00:03:38.610 --> 00:03:40.290
doesn't light up the whole circle

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:42.660
it only lights up a
certain part of the circle.

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:44.310
- I'm curious what the explanation is

00:03:44.310 --> 00:03:48.420
for gravity and things
like the coriolis effect.

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:51.030
- Well, gravity's still
technically a theory.

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:53.400
We know that there's an up and a down.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:55.170
As far as coriolis,

00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:59.085
I was in the military
and I've shot weapons

00:03:59.085 --> 00:04:03.000
and we were never once taught
to account for coriolis.

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:03.833
- What kind of weapons,

00:04:03.833 --> 00:04:06.330
if you don't mind me asking, like ICBMs?

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:08.800
- Well, when I was in the
military we shot M16's

00:04:09.739 --> 00:04:11.280
and okay the rail gun is a question

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:13.560
because it can shoot a hundred miles

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:15.150
and it's a line of sight weapon.

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:18.810
So a hundred miles using
the curvature of the earth,

00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:20.160
it just doesn't make sense

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:22.350
that they'd be able to hit the target.

00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:23.220
- With the the globe model,

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:26.070
it's like 24,000 miles the circumference?

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:28.809
- Yeah, like 25 we kind of used, yeah.

00:04:28.809 --> 00:04:29.966
- Yeah, okay.

00:04:29.966 --> 00:04:32.460
So 100 miles would be
less than 1% of that.

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:35.040
So I guess it's not much of a difference.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:36.150
Like it doesn't matter as much.

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:38.640
I guess I'm asking more in
relation to things like rockets

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:41.970
like ICBMs or airliners
and stuff like that.

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:44.190
- Airliners, if they were flying,

00:04:44.190 --> 00:04:45.570
let's say a thousand miles,

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:47.880
they would have to dip their nose down

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:50.763
to stay in a line with the globe.

00:04:51.705 --> 00:04:53.610
- So do you believe in global warming?

00:04:53.610 --> 00:04:56.430
- So I don't believe in global warming,

00:04:56.430 --> 00:04:59.910
but I do believe in a greenhouse effect.

00:04:59.910 --> 00:05:02.040
'Cause I believe we live
in a greenhouse, you know?

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:05.734
And I do think that how we
treat this place we live

00:05:05.734 --> 00:05:10.530
in is very critical to the
quality of life and other lives

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:13.620
and not just us, all the
different ecosystems and things.

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:15.120
So I'm also a vegan.

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:17.310
I know, that's.
- Nice.

00:05:17.310 --> 00:05:19.440
- Yeah, so I try to do no harm, you know?

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:22.470
- Do you believe in any
other uncommon beliefs?

00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:23.340
- Yeah, definitely.

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:25.650
I believe in giants.

00:05:25.650 --> 00:05:28.080
That there was a race

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:31.290
of humans that were very, very, very tall.

00:05:31.290 --> 00:05:32.580
- That's interesting.

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:33.840
I kind of agree with you.

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:34.673
- Really?

00:05:34.673 --> 00:05:35.506
- I'm not gonna lie.

00:05:35.506 --> 00:05:38.640
Yes, it makes sense 'cause
dinosaurs like they were so huge.

00:05:38.640 --> 00:05:39.510
So what makes you think

00:05:39.510 --> 00:05:41.875
that humans couldn't have
evolved that way either?

00:05:41.875 --> 00:05:42.708
- Totally

00:05:42.708 --> 00:05:43.541
- Yeah.

00:05:43.541 --> 00:05:44.790
- How has your idea

00:05:44.790 --> 00:05:48.240
of the earth being flat
affected your relationships?

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:51.600
- I've lost family members
who want nothing to do

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:54.840
with me because of my belief.

00:05:54.840 --> 00:05:56.613
When I first came into flat earth,

00:05:57.949 --> 00:06:00.540
I absolutely came in to try to refute it.

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:04.080
I went into this belief
kicking and screaming.

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:08.430
I never ever ever thought
I would be a flat earthers.

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:11.430
- I'm curious what your
dating life is like.

00:06:11.430 --> 00:06:13.380
- I will say I only date flat earthers.

00:06:14.243 --> 00:06:15.076
- Okay.
- Yeah.

00:06:15.076 --> 00:06:17.160
- Have you ever dated anyone
with a differing opinion?

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:20.100
I was married, so I lost my husband.

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:24.360
He was killed and so I've
just, that was about 2010.

00:06:27.032 --> 00:06:29.590
So I didn't really come
into the flat earth

00:06:30.485 --> 00:06:33.030
until around 2015, 2016

00:06:33.030 --> 00:06:35.070
where I really started questioning it.

00:06:35.070 --> 00:06:36.720
- Do you have any kids?

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:38.160
- I do, yes.

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:39.510
I have two children.

00:06:39.510 --> 00:06:43.350
My daughter who is 19 and I
have a son who will be 14.

00:06:43.350 --> 00:06:47.310
- Do they agree with
the flat earth theory?

00:06:47.310 --> 00:06:49.290
- I will say that I've given my children

00:06:49.290 --> 00:06:51.180
the opportunity to learn both.

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:53.850
My daughter really doesn't care.

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:55.890
She's like, don't talk about it mom.

00:06:55.890 --> 00:06:57.350
I don't really care, you know?

00:06:57.350 --> 00:07:01.170
So I try not to embarrass
her when she'll see stuff

00:07:01.170 --> 00:07:05.220
like this and my son is
definitely a flat earth.

00:07:05.220 --> 00:07:07.440
- What is your favorite
thing about the earth?

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:09.340
- My favorite thing about the earth

00:07:10.886 --> 00:07:13.920
is that despite anybody's
idea of what shape it is,

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:15.543
we're all here for a purpose.

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:18.240
And the relationships that we make here

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:19.800
are the most precious things.

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:22.770
The beauty in being alive here.

00:07:22.770 --> 00:07:23.610
- That's beautiful.

00:07:23.610 --> 00:07:24.443
- Thank you.

00:07:24.443 --> 00:07:26.550
- Do you think we could be more tolerant

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:27.960
of radical opinions?

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:28.980
- I think so.

00:07:28.980 --> 00:07:32.100
I think it's important
for us to be able to stand

00:07:32.100 --> 00:07:35.160
in our truth and
understand and have empathy

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:37.740
of where people are at and
why maybe they feel that way.

00:07:37.740 --> 00:07:39.960
And I may lose everything in everybody,

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:41.520
but I'm gonna still stand.

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:42.450
And thankfully we live

00:07:42.450 --> 00:07:45.510
in a country where we're
able to express openly

00:07:45.510 --> 00:07:48.280
or hopefully we can,
ideas that aren't popular,

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:49.830
and being able to stand

00:07:49.830 --> 00:07:53.100
in that truth is really what's
at the heart of the matter.

00:07:53.100 --> 00:07:54.480
- Okay.

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:55.313
- Hi.
- Hi.

00:07:56.220 --> 00:07:57.338
- Thank you.

00:07:57.338 --> 00:07:59.070
- Thank you for sharing.

00:07:59.070 --> 00:07:59.903
- You're so sweet.

00:07:59.903 --> 00:08:00.870
- Information to me.

00:08:00.870 --> 00:08:02.400
- I loved all the questions.

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:03.731
- Thank you for answering.

00:08:03.731 --> 00:08:06.623
- Oh she had a nicer mic than me.

00:08:06.623 --> 00:08:08.400
- [Speaker] Parents are heroes.

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:09.400
Right, you're right.

